{# Bag slots (cols × rows × bags levels from build.py), row-major numbering.
   Level L holds cells (L-1)*cols*rows+1 … L*cols*rows; only the level matching
   attr_bag_level is displayed (CSS). The band's rightmost stitched column is
   the pouch: consuming an "extra_bag" item there unlocks the next level. #}
{% set per_level = cols * rows %}
{% for i in range(1, per_level * bags + 1) %}
{% set level = ((i - 1) // per_level) + 1 %}
{% set cell = (i - 1) % per_level %}
  <div class="sheet-slot sheet-slot--bag_{{ i }} sheet-bag-cell-{{ cell }} sheet-bag-level-{{ level }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="attr_bag_{{ i }}" value="" />
    <span class="sheet-item-icon"></span>
    <button type="action" name="act_slot_bag_{{ i }}"></button>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
  {# The pouch: drop an extra_bag item here to unlock the next level. #}
  <button type="action" class="sheet-pouch" name="act_slot_pouch"></button>
  {# Level navigation arrows, living on the pouch. #}
  <button type="action" class="sheet-bag-nav sheet-bag-nav--up" name="act_bag_up"></button>
  <button type="action" class="sheet-bag-nav sheet-bag-nav--down" name="act_bag_down"></button>
  {# Trash: visible only while an item is in hand — deletes it outright. #}
  <button type="action" class="sheet-trash" name="act_trash"></button>
  {# Read a scroll: holding a "scroll" item (see items.json's scroll-*
     entries) and clicking this reads it — 1d100 vs its own fixed
     spell_casting (NOT the player's live casting stat), labeled with its
     spell_label, then the scroll is consumed. Visible only while holding a
     scroll (see inventory-slots.css.j2), same as the trash's hand-gated
     visibility. #}
  <button type="action" class="sheet-read-scroll" name="act_read_scroll"></button>
  <div class="sheet-statbar sheet-statbar--read-scroll">Lire le parchemin</div>
  {# Consommer: holding a food/drinks/potions item (items.json's effect field)
     and clicking this emotes "/me mange : Pomme" and empties the case — both
     done by !arxconsume in arx-mod.js, exactly like the loot panel's Prendre
     buttons. Neither half can be done from the sheet: a worker's startRoll
     renders a roll template and never an emote, and Roll20 does not fire
     clicked: for a type="roll" button (tested in game — the item stayed in
     hand). The label lives on a <span>, not in the button: base.css blanks
     the font on every roll button to kill Roll20's d20 badge. Shares the
     Lire button's spot, the two can never both show. #}
  <div class="sheet-consume">
    <span class="sheet-consume-face">Consommer</span>
    <button type="roll" name="act_consume" value="!arxconsume"></button>
  </div>
